<title>UK: Chelsea sign new sponsorship deal.</title>
<headline>Chelsea sign new sponsorship deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>English F.A. Cup finalists Chelsea Village Plc have signed a new four-year sponsorship deal with car windscreen company Autoglass, the club said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Chelsea gave no financial details of the deal but London's Evening Standard said it would be worth a total of 4.5 million stg.</p>
<p>The London football club are currently sponsored by Coors lager but owners Scottish Courage do not intend to extend the three-year agreement when it expires at the end of the season.</p>
<p>-- Keith Weir, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8793</p>
